Keep a reference whose intersection type needed no box adaptation

scala/scala3 #27394 made box adaptation pull the capture sets out of an
intersection or union of capturing types before adapting it. The rewritten
type was returned whether or not anything was then adapted, so the caller,
which keeps the reference it was given only if its widened type comes back
unchanged, replaced every stable reference of such a type by the type. A
path through the reference became a projection:

    case gathering: Gathering => keep[gathering.Self](gathering.gathered(Nil))

    Found:    (Parsing & Gathering)#Self
    Required: gathering.Self

for a variable bound by a typed pattern, whose type is the scrutinee's
meeting the pattern's. The type is now returned as it was where the
adaptation changed nothing, as the case for a match type beside it does.

Found in Soundness's xylophone and stratiform.

